@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+apiVersion: v1
+kind: Service
+metadata:
+  name: demosrv
+  namespace: traffic-sim
+  annotations:
+    cloud.google.com/backend-config: '{"default": "demosrv-http-bc", "ports": {"http": "demosrv-http-bc", "ws": "demosrv-ws-bc"}}'
+    # BackendConfig only takes effect on container-native (NEG) backends;
+    # state it explicitly rather than inheriting cluster defaults.
+    cloud.google.com/neg: '{"ingress": true}'
+spec:
+  selector:
+    app: demosrv
+  ports:
+    - name: http
+      port: 80
+      targetPort: http
+    - name: ws
+      port: 8443
+      targetPort: ws
diff --git a/docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0020-demosrv-public-deployment.md b/docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0020-demosrv-public-deployment.md
index 5d46de6df26ccec9a00b9e6ebf241f941056242a..1d6734a8767af2fa324349fee771c01ccf855dc2 100644
--- a/docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0020-demosrv-public-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0020-demosrv-public-deployment.md
@@ -127,8 +127,8 @@ demosrv gains four flags (`engine/cmd/demosrv`, deploy.go):
 - The ws port still binds inside the pod on `-ws`; the LB (or a
   sidecar) owns TLS. demosrv remains plain HTTP/ws internally — no TLS
   stack enters this codebase.
-- Deploy manifests (image build, Ingress, token plumbing) live outside
-  the repo; this ADR covers only the demosrv-side contract. `-autostart`
+- Deploy manifests (image build, Ingress, token plumbing) live in
+  `deploy/` (this ADR covers only the demosrv-side contract). `-autostart`
   is ONE-SHOT: a demo that crashes after a successful start leaves the
   pod idle — crash recovery is the manifests' job (K8s liveness/pod
   restart), not a demosrv supervisor loop.
